{"title":"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(somewhat_fake)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (somewhat fake)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Extend the square pattern of 8 black and 17 white square tiles by attaching a border of black tiles around the square. What is the ratio of black tiles to white tiles in the extended pattern?<br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a24e23a268700a40b52b1b449dac9c6d2ec80a4e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] filldraw((0,0)--(5,0)--(5,5)--(0,5)--cycle,white,black); filldraw((1,1)--(4,1)--(4,4)--(1,4)--cycle,mediumgray,black); filldraw((2,2)--(3,2)--(3,3)--(2,3)--cycle,white,black); draw((4,0)--(4,5)); draw((3,0)--(3,5)); draw((2,0)--(2,5)); draw((1,0)--(1,5)); draw((0,4)--(5,4)); draw((0,3)--(5,3)); draw((0,2)--(5,2)); draw((0,1)--(5,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/3/f43e2c44d68652dff0ac3222719f13e854c00941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }8:17 \\qquad\\textbf{(B) }25:49 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) }36:25 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) }32:17 \\qquad\\textbf{(E) }36:17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"556\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>One way of approaching this is drawing the next circle of boxes around the current square.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d5e03ab002d178fce4ca257ee3d4fff4e3c31f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] filldraw((-1,-1)--(6,-1)--(6,6)--(-1,6)--cycle,mediumgray,black); filldraw((0,0)--(5,0)--(5,5)--(0,5)--cycle,white,black); filldraw((1,1)--(4,1)--(4,4)--(1,4)--cycle,mediumgray,black); filldraw((2,2)--(3,2)--(3,3)--(2,3)--cycle,white,black); draw((4,-1)--(4,6)); draw((3,-1)--(3,6)); draw((2,-1)--(2,6)); draw((1,-1)--(1,6)); draw((-1,4)--(6,4)); draw((-1,3)--(6,3)); draw((-1,2)--(6,2)); draw((-1,1)--(6,1)); draw((0,-1)--(0,6)); draw((-1,5)--(6,5)); draw((-1,0)--(6,0)); draw((5,-1)--(5,6)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\nWe can now count the number of black and white tiles; 32 black tiles and 17 white tiles. This means the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/921e3060f9fbb5758e6f59e03606acc8bf39b152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }32:17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we did not want to draw a diagram though that is probably simpler in this case, we can imagine the last border of black tiles. We see that each side length (if the side length of a square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />) increases by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> each time we go out one layer. Therefore, we know that the next border will have a side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. That border has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b62471f829da9a8237771fa50cd2b295c8fb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^2-5^2=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> black squares in it. The other black border has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/2/d227bad85d4934b6a71464b5a4b3cf01cd995eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^2-1^2=8$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> squares in it, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> black squares in all. The other ones must all be white, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23fa6d8bd8a3e891fd1f683ee7ad0f99ab360007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49-32=17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"101\" height=\"13\" /> white squares. Thus, we get our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/921e3060f9fbb5758e6f59e03606acc8bf39b152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }32:17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28somewhat_fake.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(somewhat_fake)\">Solution 3 (somewhat fake)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (somewhat fake)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that in total, once we add the border there will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/026bb71c09708994ead7a4ee100a03960a87c4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> squares total. So far as there is only one option that sums to 49 and we know that there are an integer number of boxes, it has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/921e3060f9fbb5758e6f59e03606acc8bf39b152.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }32:17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" />. ~math_genius_11\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6XNr5HWgMdI\">https://youtu.be/6XNr5HWgMdI</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 8\">2011 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2011\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=